# Deploy Workflow

## What yui needs

1. **New code reaches the live site.** A change that affects served files must
   land on `master` (direct push or merged PR). That triggers GitHub Actions →
   rsync → https://fuseki.net/music8899b/. Reload the page to see it.
2. **Know which build is loaded.** The header version label and every asset
   `?v=N` share one number from `VERSION` / `app-version.js`. After deploy,
   reload and check the header.

Docs/rules-only pushes are skipped by Actions (`paths-ignore`); they never
change the live site.

## Direct-to-master (default)

When yui directs mei to make changes:

1. Work on `master` directly — no feature branches, no PR review ceremony.
2. Commit with clear messages (still multiple small commits, not one blob).
3. Push `master` once for the ship (see version rules below).

If the cloud agent system assigns a feature branch, override it: check out
`master`, make changes there, push `master`. Cursor's PR diff pane stays empty
under master-direct — that is expected; review via the agent transcript or
GitHub commits on `master`.

### Exceptions

- If yui explicitly asks for a PR or branch, do that instead (merge to `master`
  so auto-deploy still runs; auto-merge is fine — yui should not have to
  babysit GitHub review).
- If mei already committed on a feature branch before seeing this rule, merge
  into `master`, push `master`, clean up the branch.
- If mei are genuinely uncertain about a change, ask before pushing to master.

## Version bump

Run `./bump-version.sh` **once per user-facing ship**, in the **same push** as
the change. Never push a bump-only commit: it still deploys new `?v=` / header
numbers with no real code change, which misleads yui about what "new" means
and races other agents.

```
work, commit…  →  ./bump-version.sh  →  commit version files with the change  →  push master once  →  deploy live as vN
                                                                                                      →  reload; header shows vN
```

**Skip the bump** when the push only touches rsync-excluded paths (docs,
tests, `.cursor/`, scripts, etc.).

**Concurrent agents:** before the ship push, `git fetch origin master` and
rebase (or reset+cherry-pick onto origin). If `VERSION` moved, re-run
`./bump-version.sh` so the ship is exactly one past origin, then push once
with content + version together.

## Pipeline (reference)

Push to `master` (when not paths-ignored) → typecheck → lint → `npm test` →
rsync `--delete` (excludes docs/tests/tooling; list shared with `deploy.sh`) →
live. Manual: `./deploy.sh`. Details: [docs/setup.md](docs/setup.md).
